91:Fig. 1. Overview of the dataset and analysis workflow. A total of 380 brain imaging data were initially collected from two datasets: Dataset 1 (n = 311) and Dataset 2 (n = 69). Due to low image quality, 16 images were excluded from Dataset 1 and 2 images from Dataset 2, resulting in a total of 362 remaining images. Dataset 1 (n = 295, TDC) was used to construct growth curve models of corpus callosum morphometrics, focusing on age-related variations and developmental trends. Dataset 2 (n = 41, TDC; n = 26, ASD) was used to validate the classifier by assessing the role of growth curves in identifying corpus callosum abnormalities associated with ASD.
